{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SGTqUPPbJ9J5GoYPQcqEnT","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t+++\n2\tid = \"WI-976\"\n3\ttitle = \"The perspective-record sidecar retires and the 2026-09-06 SN-036 ruling applies here: an SN to SR round's sitting and author briefs carry the applicable hats' questions, and the sitting's verdict names each hat's outcome\"\n4\tworkstream = \"process\"\n5\tsr_refs = [\"SR-161\", \"SR-186\"]\n6\tspecref = \"docs/plans/2026-10-11-review-churn/README.md#14-retire-the-perspective-record-sidecar-apply-the-2026-09-06-hat-ruling-here\"\n7\tbuildtier = \"medium\"\n8\tsafety_class = \"ordinary\"\n9\tpriority = 5\n10\tplanmode = \"single\"\n11\t+++\n12\t\n13\t## Context\n14\t\n15\tFiled by hand in headless leg 19 (2026-10-25) from the review-churn plan's\n16\titem 14, the queue's row P3 (`docs/handoff-2026-10-11-attended-coordinator.md`):\n17\t\"retire the perspective-record sidecar, the SN-036 ruling's four row acts,\n18\tthe hat questions in the SN -> SR briefs. One sitting, one owner act.\n19\tBefore item 5's migration and the FileBackup re-sync.\" A planner-drafter\n20\tread the plan's item 14 and its rulings and confirmed them against trunk at\n21\t`2695213c6`.\n22\t\n23\tThe rulings behind it: the owner's direction of 2026-10-13 (revision 21:\n24\tthe 2026-09-06 SN-036 ruling stands); revision 22 (wire the hat questions\n25\tinto the coordinator's briefs, and delete the existing sidecar); revision\n26\t23 (the hat block only for decomposition rounds); revision 24 (the hats\n27\tapply when a need is decomposed into SRs); revision 25 (SAFETY leaves this\n28\trepo's roster); revision 30 (SR-161's title, the slot grammar); revision 31\n29\t(`contract_split` is read only at its tip, `961f9e47`). The ruling's own\n30\ttext is the 2026-09-06 fragment added at `f6c7360f`\n31\t(`docs/log.d/2026-09-06-sn036-owner-ruling.md` there); at the tip it is\n32\tfolded into `contract_split`'s `docs/log.md`, under \"2026-09-06 — SN-036 /\n33\tSR-161 owner ruling: review pass, not a guard\", and closes: \"Do NOT build\n34\t`hats_no_finding`, a sidecar record, or a coverage check.\"\n35\t\n36\t**Anchor.** SR-161 (Approved), under SN-036 (Approved). SR-186, the other\n37\tSR that TC-211 verifies, does not change.\n38\t\n39\t**What exists today (verified on trunk at filing).**\n40\t\n41\t- The tool: the roster reader `project-trajectory/scripts/hats.py` has a\n42\t  `record` subcommand (its record section, its docstring and usage lines),\n43\t  tested by `tests/test_hats_record.py`; nothing outside these two files\n44\t  calls a record symbol, and no hook, CI workflow or `check.py` step runs\n45\t  it (warn-first).\n46\t- The rows: LLR-297 and TC-312 (both Approved); LLR-183's detail (\"The\n47\t  machine-readable half of the perspective record\" ... \"the no-finding half\n48\t  is a per-decomposition artifact, built under LLR-297\"); TC-211's `inputs`\n49\t  naming the sidecar; SR-161's requirement, acceptance and `coincident`\n50\t  asking for the record; SN-036's acceptance (\"a machine-readable record\",\n51\t  \"a check reports\"); IF-133's `data` cell listing `load`, which only the\n52\t  record's spine index calls.\n53\t- The instructions that ask for the record: PROCESS.md section 1's sentence\n54\t  \"Each decomposition also leaves a perspective record beside it\";\n55\t  `project-trajectory/prompts/spine-questions.md` (c3); the template\n56\t  roster's \"THE PER-DECOMPOSITION RECORD\" paragraph; this repo's roster's\n57\t  \"WHAT IS NOT BUILT YET\" paragraph; the RESYNC entry \"The\n58\t  per-decomposition perspective record [since 9233772b]\".\n59\t- The generated pages that show it: `docs/cli-reference.md`,\n60\t  `docs/requirements/components.derived.toml`, `docs/test/report.md`.\n61\t\n62\t**What the plan's evidence missed (found at filing; each joins this row's\n63\tscope).**\n64\t\n65\t- **Seven sidecars, not one.** Beside\n66\t  `docs/ai-template-redesign-2026-09-05-codex/DECOMPOSITION-AMENDMENTS.perspectives.toml`,\n67\t  the spine author wrote six between 2026-10-21 and 10-23, under\n68\t  `docs/plans/WI-850/` (two), `WI-957/`, `WI-958/`, `WI-960/` and `WI-961/`.\n69\t- **In practice it is a hold.** The coordinator recipe tells lanes to write\n70\t  the record \"until plan item 14 retires the sidecar\" (the\n71\t  `coordinator-cycle` recipes, three copies), and first-approval sittings\n72\t  have returned derived SRs for lacking one (wi-957 sitting 003, wi-958\n73\t  sitting 005, wi-960 sitting 005). No code gates on the record; a sitting\n74\t  reading (c3) and SR-161 does.\n75\t- **TC-211's rubric and procedure ask for it too:**\n76\t  `docs/rubrics/decomposition-proportionality.md` anchors R1 and B1, and\n77\t  `docs/test/inspection-procedures.md` (the proportionality procedure, its\n78\t  result section, still reading INCOMPLETE 2026-09-06 although the\n79\t  2026-10-03 pass is on record, and the closing paragraph of \"Bounded\n80\t  abnormal inputs\").\n81\t- **Removing SAFETY changes tests:** the roster tests pin one name list for\n82\t  both rosters and read SAFETY from the live roster, and the roster header\n83\t  counts \"Sixteen hats today\".\n84\t- **The coordinator's sittings are combined sittings,** composed section by\n85\t  section through each kind's assembler, so a slot in the two templates\n86\t  reaches them, and one sitting can compose both kinds.\n87\t- **The author prompt has no path for a computed block:** the coordinator's\n88\t  prompt filler only substitutes literal values, and the prompt tests pin\n89\t  the spine-author template's slot set.\n90\t- **An amended need is not reached today:** the planner briefs'\n91\t  applicability function reaches needs only through the row's SR-Refs and\n92\t  a SpecRef naming one SN, so a round that amends a need must pass that\n93\t  need in as a parent context.\n94\t- **Composed sitting briefs are not committed** (a lane commits only the\n95\t  verdict and its binding), while TC-211's procedure reads the sample's\n96\t  brief.\n97\t- **No `contract_split` wording exists for SR-161's `coincident` cell**\n98\t  (WI-655 added those cells here after the split), so that rewrite is this\n99\t  lane's own text.\n100\t\n101\t**Deliverables and landing order (S1).** One row, kept whole on the owner's\n102\tdirection (\"one sitting, one owner act\"), in this lane order:\n103\t\n104\t1. The ruling record: a log fragment carrying the 2026-09-06 decision, its\n105\t   four acts and its closing line, citing `f6c7360f` and `contract_split`'s\n106\t   `docs/log.md` heading, plus the 2026-10-13 direction and the revision 25\n107\t   SAFETY ruling. SN-036's act cites this fragment directly, with no open\n108\t   item.\n109\t2. The spine change set, authored at the intent turn: SN-036, SR-161,\n110\t   LLR-183, TC-178 and TC-211 amended; LLR-297 and TC-312 retired; one new\n111\t   LLR under SR-161 and one TC for the sitting brief's hat block; IF-133's\n112\t   `data` cell amended.\n113\t3. The retirement: code, tests, records, instructions, generated pages, and\n114\t   SAFETY in this repo's roster.\n115\t4. The hat block in the two sitting templates' composition and in the\n116\t   spine-author prompt.\n117\t5. SN-036's act, which is the owner's (Done-when, \"The owner-held step\"),\n118\t   with the sitting's other acts.\n119\t6. TC-211's re-judge after the acts, against this lane's own checkpoint\n120\t   sitting, an SN to SR round (SN-036 is amended) and the first round to\n121\t   use deliverable 4.\n122\t\n123\tDeliverables 3, 4 and 6 hang from SR-161's amended text, which the one\n124\tsitting judges, and 6's sample is 4's first use. A split would add a second sitting\n125\tand, between its landings, leave Approved SR-161 asking for a record that\n126\tno longer exists, or stating a brief the coordinator's path does not\n127\tcompose.\n128\t\n129\t**Authority (S2).** No deliverable gives a file authority over a hold, an\n130\tact or a ga