ed whose text is amended, and any other judged set carries\n190\t  no perspective question; the applicable set is the union of the\n191\t  perspectives whose condition holds for each of the round's parent needs\n192\t  (each amended need, and each need a judged system requirement names),\n193\t  each need widened by the work item's declared tags and evaluated alone;\n194\t  the questions fill the perspective slot only where the sitting's template\n195\t  declares it, and a template that declares none composes unchanged; a\n196\t  sitting composing several judgement kinds carries them once; an absent\n197\t  roster yields the roster's no-perspective line, and a roster that exists\n198\t  and cannot be read refuses the composition, naming the roster.\n199\t\n200\t**Unchanged, on purpose:** `Hat-Refs` (LLR-183, LLR-202; TC-178, TC-198)\n201\tand the planner's `{{HAT_QUESTIONS}}` path; whether LLRs keep the\n202\t`hat_refs` cell (the plan's separate question); the places that say\n203\t\"perspective record\" but mean `Hat-Refs`; and historical records (reviews,\n204\tdecisions, logs, handoffs, call logs, the archive, closed specs).\n205\t\n206\t**The six lane-authored sidecars** (a call the plan did not answer): the\n207\truling deleted the one record a builder wrote after the fact; these six\n208\twere written by the spine author and landed sittings cite them. This spec's\n209\tdefault: they stay, as inert lane records under `docs/plans/`, outside the\n210\tlive surface (coordinator-2026-10-25 D-003, for the owner to confirm or\n211\toverrule).\n212\t\n213\t## Done-when\n214\t\n215\t**The ruling record**\n216\t- [ ] The log fragment of deliverable 1 is committed before any row text\n217\t  changes.\n218\t\n219\t**The spine** (judged at one checkpoint sitting, top-down)\n220\t- [ ] SN-036, SR-161, LLR-183, TC-178 and TC-211 carry `contract_split`'s\n221\t  meaning, SR-161's rationale and `coincident` aside, as proposed above:\n222\t  TC-178's `expected` is split (LLR-183's `Hat-Refs` mechanics here,\n223\t  SR-161's acceptance inspected by TC-211); TC-211 verifies SR-161 and\n224\t  SR-186, inspects one actual completed decomposition review record, and\n225\t  its `inputs` name that record and its brief and no sidecar, its other\n226\t  cells staying.\n227\t- [ ] LLR-297 and TC-312 are retired, each with its retirement record, at\n228\t  the sitting that rules those amendments.\n229\t- [ ] One new LLR under SR-161 states the sitting brief's hat block, and one\n230\t  TC verifies it.\n231\t- [ ] IF-133's `data` cell no longer lists `load`.\n232\t- [ ] `docs/test/inspection-procedures.md` takes `contract_split`'s\n233\t  proportionality procedure and its \"missing perspective outcome\" abnormal\n234\t  input; the 2026-09-06 INCOMPLETE result stays as history.\n235\t- [ ] `docs/rubrics/decomposition-proportionality.md` R1 and B1 ask for the\n236\t  review record's outcomes, not a record producer.\n237\t\n238\t**The retirement**\n239\t- [ ] The roster reader's `record` command and its test module are removed,\n240\t  with every symbol, import and docstring line only they used.\n241\t- [ ] `DECOMPOSITION-AMENDMENTS.perspectives.toml` and its pointer paragraph\n242\t  in `DECOMPOSITION-AMENDMENTS.md` go.\n243\t- [ ] No instruction asks for the record: PROCESS.md section 1's record\n244\t  sentence goes; `spine-questions.md` (c3) becomes the ruling's rule (the\n245\t  review record names each applicable hat's outcome, and a missing outcome\n246\t  is a review finding, never a coverage gate); both roster headers state\n247\t  the same rule, and `docs/requirements/hats.toml`'s \"WHAT IS NOT BUILT\n248\t  YET\" paragraph goes; the coordinator recipe's perspective-record line\n249\t  goes, in all three copies.\n250\t- [ ] SAFETY leaves `docs/requirements/hats.toml`, citing the revision 25\n251\t  ruling: its header count and its open SAFETY call close, the shipped\n252\t  template keeps SAFETY, and the live and template name pins in the rost